Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

Start infrastructure

For sync-only test:
docker compose up -d neo4j
For Kafka test:
docker compose up -d zookeeper kafka neo4j kafka-init
Pick one timestamp (same for both runs, rounded to 15 min)
Example: 2026-04-14T12:15

Run sync baseline
python main_sync.py --timestamp 2026-04-14T12:15
or via harness:
python benchmark_experiment.py --mode sync --timestamp 2026-04-14T12:15

Run Kafka mode
Before each Kafka run, reset broker data to avoid consuming old topic history:
docker compose down -v
docker compose up -d zookeeper kafka neo4j kafka-init
Then run:
python benchmark_experiment.py --mode kafka --timestamp 2026-04-14T12:15

Compare outputs

Sync summary comes from main_sync.py
Kafka and sync benchmark timing comes from benchmark_experiment.py
Use the final INFO lines (elapsed seconds, processed/skipped counts) to compare latency and throughput.
